# vpn-eta configuration — copy to ~/.config/vpn-eta/config and edit.
#
# This file is sourced by the plugin as a shell fragment, so it is `NAME=value`,
# one per line, quoted when the value has spaces. Everything here is optional;
# delete a line to go back to the default shown.
#
# Why a file and not your shell profile: SwiftBar starts plugins from launchd,
# which does not read ~/.zshrc or ~/.zprofile. A variable exported there reaches
# a terminal run of the plugin and never reaches the menu bar. This file reaches
# both. ($VPN_ETA_CONFIG points somewhere else if you prefer.)
#
# Watching two gateways: copy the plugin under a second name and give it a
# config named after it. vpn-eta-lab.1m.sh reads vpn-eta-lab.config from this
# directory if it exists, and this shared file otherwise — no edit to either
# copy required.

# ── Which VPN ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Which saved Cisco profile "Start new session" connects to. Only needed when
# Cisco Secure Client has more than one — with a single profile the plugin uses
# it. Accepts a profile name or a full URL, and is passed to Cisco untouched.
#VPN_ETA_HOST="vpn.example.com"

# Where the Cisco CLI lives, if it is not at one of the two standard paths
# (/opt/cisco/secureclient/bin/vpn, then /opt/cisco/anyconnect/bin/vpn).
#VPN_ETA_VPN_BIN="/opt/cisco/secureclient/bin/vpn"

# ── What the menu bar shows ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The word in front of the countdown. Worth changing if you run this plugin
# twice against two gateways: "Work 6h 20m" and "Lab 2h 05m" beat two "VPN"s.
# An emoji is the narrowest label there is, and an empty string removes the
# label entirely — both are the lever to pull if the item is too wide.
#   VPN_ETA_LABEL="VPN"   ->  VPN 6h 20m
#   VPN_ETA_LABEL="🦍"    ->  🦍 6h 20m
#   VPN_ETA_LABEL=""      ->  6h 20m
#VPN_ETA_LABEL="VPN"

# Drop the minutes from the MENU BAR while more than an hour is left: "6h"
# rather than "6h 20m". Under an hour the minutes are the whole point, so they
# stay. The menu itself always shows the exact figure. Rounds down, so the menu
# bar never claims more time than you have.
#   VPN_ETA_COMPACT=1     ->  🦍 6h   ... and 🦍 45m under the hour
#VPN_ETA_COMPACT=

# Countdown colour, in minutes remaining: red at or below the first, orange at
# or below the second, green above. Separate from the notification marks below,
# because a colour you glance at and an alert that interrupts you are not the
# same decision.
#VPN_ETA_CRITICAL_MINUTES=15
#VPN_ETA_WARN_MINUTES=60

# ── Notifications ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Minutes-remaining marks that raise a notification, high to low. Each fires
# once per session. Set to "" to switch notifications off entirely.
#VPN_ETA_NOTIFY_MARKS="60 15"

# ── Session log ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# How many lines of history.log to keep.
#VPN_ETA_HISTORY_LINES=500

# Where the plugin keeps its state and log. The default is not the path below:
# under SwiftBar it is the per-plugin data directory SwiftBar hands out,
# ~/Library/Application Support/SwiftBar/Plugins/vpn-eta.1m.sh, and only a run
# outside SwiftBar falls back to ~/Library/Application Support/vpn-eta. Set this
# to make a terminal run and the menu bar share one history.
# NOTE: ./uninstall.sh reads this, so a custom path is still cleaned up.
#VPN_ETA_STATE_DIR="$HOME/Library/Application Support/vpn-eta"

# ── Timing ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Seconds to wait for the Cisco CLI before giving up on one call. The CLI talks
# to a daemon and can hang; this is the watchdog.
#VPN_ETA_TIMEOUT=12

# How long a countdown extrapolated from the last confirmed reading stays
# trustworthy, in minutes. Past this the plugin says it does not know rather
# than showing a number it cannot stand behind.
#VPN_ETA_STALE_LIMIT=45

# Grace period, in seconds, during which a disconnect is treated as one you
# asked for rather than a drop worth announcing.
#VPN_ETA_TEARDOWN_GRACE=300

# How long to wait for a freshly connected session to report its countdown:
# attempts, and seconds between them.
#VPN_ETA_CONNECT_ATTEMPTS=15
#VPN_ETA_CONNECT_SLEEP=2
